  "original_patch_has_test_hunk": true,
  "source_conclusion": "The complete two-file/three-hunk menu lazy-view fix is adapted to the locally owned historical menu. The earlier immediate-overlay-detach implementation could not paint an exit; that defect was repaired separately while preserving the Material16 template/style and public constructor contracts. Current semantic close releases focus/input immediately, then only the current owner detaches overlay and lazy content on void/completion; transfer cancels old removal and releases the old view before attaching the new owner. Genuine Core/RxJS constructor protocols exercise lifetime/reentry but are not native or packed qualification. The required packed case observes actual query membership, directive destruction, distinct re-created items and two-trigger transfer. All native CSS exit cases and global motion gates remain independently mandatory; no painting/timing, hydration, floor, security or G11 pass follows from this source conclusion.",
  "decision": "The complete two-file/three-hunk menu lazy-view fix is adapted to the locally owned historical menu. The earlier immediate-overlay-detach implementation could not paint an exit; that defect was repaired separately while preserving the Material16 template/style and public constructor contracts. Current semantic close releases focus/input immediately, then only the current owner detaches overlay and lazy content on void/completion; transfer cancels old removal and releases the old view before attaching the new owner. Genuine Core/RxJS constructor protocols exercise lifetime/reentry but are not native or packed qualification. The required packed case observes actual query membership, directive destruction, distinct re-created items and two-trigger transfer. All native CSS exit cases and global motion gates remain independently mandatory; no painting/timing, hydration, floor, security or G11 pass follows from this source conclusion.",
  "hunk_reviews": [
    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/material/menu/menu-trigger.ts",
      "header": "@@ -368,10 +368,14 @@ export class MatMenuTrigger implements AfterContentInit, OnDestroy {",
      "judgment": "The runtime hunk restores lazyContent.detach after owner animation completion and in the immediate other-owner path. Owned _destroyMenu now retains the rendered attachment until a valid void/completion and guards generation/ownership; _detachMenu releases only its own attachment and avoids destroying reentrant new-owner content. The separately reviewed 18 constructor cases/14 mutants cover fallback, reopen, transfer and teardown. Actual packed view destruction and all native exit rendering still have to pass."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/material/menu/menu.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -15,9 +15,11 @@ import {ScrollDispatcher, ViewportRuler} from '@angular/cdk/scrolling';",
      "judgment": "Directive and OnDestroy imports support an actual lifecycle witness in the upstream regression. The owned packed MenuDestroyProbe is instantiated alongside real legacy items inside matMenuContent and counts Angular destruction, rather than replacing ngOnDestroy with a spy or manually emitting a completion event."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 3,
      "file": "src/material/menu/menu.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -1219,6 +1221,40 @@ describe('MatMenu', () => {",
      "judgment": "The original regression opens a two-item lazy menu, then requires both query disappearance and two destruction calls after close. The packed case preserves those observations, adds a second creation/destruction cycle and real shared-panel transfer, and requires connected-node counts and actual trigger output sequences. Provider-disabled packed behavior is not used to certify enabled CSS painting; the unchanged native roster remains required."
    }
  ],
